### Banking API requests for IntelliJ's built-in HTTP client.
### Start the API first (run BankingApiApp), then click the green arrow next to a request.
### Run them top to bottom: login saves the token, and the later requests use it.
### The admin requests need the API started with --admin-token, and the same value below.

@adminToken = replace-with-the-admin-token-you-started-the-api-with

### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### Register alice
POST http://localhost:8080/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "fullName": "Alice Doe",
  "password": "Passw0rd1"
}

### Register bob (the second account to transfer to)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "fullName": "Bob Roe",
  "password": "Passw0rd1"
}

### Log in as alice (saves the token for the requests below)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Passw0rd1"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### My account
GET http://localhost:8080/api/account
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deposit
POST http://localhost:8080/api/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 250.75
}

### Deposit with an Idempotency-Key. Run this twice: the second answer is identical and no money is added again.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 0b9c1f6e-6d52-4a43-9b7e-1f0f1e2d3c4b
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 10
}

### The API's own OpenAPI description
GET http://localhost:8080/api/openapi.yaml

### Withdraw
POST http://localhost:8080/api/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 20
}

### Transfer to bob (bob's account number is shown when you register him)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toAccountNumber": "1000000002",
  "amount": 50
}

### Transaction history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change password (other sessions end; this one stays signed in)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "oldPassword": "Passw0rd1",
  "newPassword": "N3wPassword"
}

### ADMIN: unlock a locked user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/unlock
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice"
}

### ADMIN: audit log for one user (leave out username for everyone)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/audit?username=alice&limit=20
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

### Log out (the token stops working)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
